define phrase throne-stub, stopping while the ball is open or the ball is decided
  (TODO during play-testing — The throne stands at the head of the room, and
  the Queen in it, and beside the throne, alive, with his hands folded behind
  his back like any courtier, stands Bobby. Pieter is with him. Bobby's eyes
