## `JE1` (`story.ni:11266`), unasked, once.

define phrase jacobs-je1-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — 'Well now, look who we have here,' says a gruff
  voice behind you. 'You must be the girl my son helped out of prison
  recently.' It is the jailhouse face, and then it isn't: older, richer, the
  father. Jacobs the Elder has informants everywhere and no plans to reveal
  you to Fossville; he is a businessman, with many diversified interests. He
  walks you through the room with his eyes — the Queen, the Princess working
  the crowd, the Duke and Duchess of Inhyron, the Baron of Amhyron, the Earl
  of Bresa. 'Those are the players of the game in this room, and you will have
  to spar with all of them if you want to win. You're a long shot. It's all
  about how many allies you have.' He pats your arm. 'Well, that should be
  enough to get you started. Good luck, my girl.')
end phrase

## `JE12-JE20` (`story.ni:11293-11311`), on `talk to` after.

define phrase jacobs-je12-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — 'Back for more, hmm?' says Jacobs the Elder.
  Fossville is sending a message, he thinks; maybe he planned this whole thing
  just to trap you. The old Duke left himself open. The Queen merely watches
  the field; the Princess is an opportunist; the Duke of Inhyron a stuffed
  shirt and a hypocrite; Amhyron honest and good-hearted but bound to the
  Inhyrons; and Bresa a fat idiot — ignore him. 'Always a pleasure, my dear
  girl.')
end phrase

