define phrase priestess-asks-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — The Priestess comes to you through the crowd,
  and the crowd does not seem to see her come. 'Jacqueline,' she says. 'Come
  with me.' It is not a question, and you find that it was never going to be.
  Something in you has already stood up and started walking. You go, alone.)
end phrase

define phrase queen-leaves-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — The Queen rises and leaves without a word, and
  Bobby goes with her, and does not look back. One by one the faces in the
  room turn away from you. Nobody will meet your eye; nobody will speak. You
  stand alone in the middle of the Baron's ballroom with the Duke's letter in
  your hand, and it is over.)
end phrase

