  The Earl of Bresa has a bald head and a huge, curly, red beard. His
  lavish, colorful clothes are stained with wine and food. He laughs too
  loudly and has a habit of putting his greasy fingers on other guests —
  usually a friendly slap on the back for the men, elsewhere for the women.
  Despite Jacobs' warning, you find yourself liking him immediately.

